  ===================================================================
   LINEAR ELASTICITY BENCHMARK 5 — CONSTANT-STRESS PATCH TEST
  ===================================================================

   PROBLEM DEFINITION
     The fundamental FE verification test. A unit cube is meshed with
     2x2x2 hexahedra and its single interior node is deliberately
     perturbed off the regular grid. A linear displacement field
         u = (a*x, b*y, c*z)
     is imposed on EVERY boundary node. A correct element must then
     reproduce a CONSTANT strain/stress state throughout, regardless
     of the interior distortion.
       E = 1.0, nu = 0.3
       a = 0.01 (strain_xx), b = 0.0 (strain_yy), c = 0.0 (strain_zz)
       interior node perturbed by 0.1*h

   BOUNDARY CONDITIONS
     all boundary nodes : prescribed u = (a*x, b*y, c*z)

   EXACT SOLUTION  (constant everywhere)
     Lame parameters:  lambda = 0.576923,  mu = 0.384615
     Strain:  eps_xx=0.01  eps_yy=0  eps_zz=0
     Stress:  sig_xx=0.0134615  sig_yy=0.00576923  sig_zz=0.00576923
     PASS criteria (to machine precision):
       - interior node displaces to u=(a*x,b*y,c*z) at its position
       - every element reports the constant stress above
  -->
